==============================================================================
Deliberately not shipped
==============================================================================

pdfjs-dist carries more than the viewer takes. These are never copied into
the build and are a 404 on the site (docs/pdf-viewer.md § Licences):

- The Liberation fonts, standard_fonts/LiberationSans-*.ttf, and
  standard_fonts/LICENSE_LIBERATION: GPL-2.0 with a font exception. Text in
  a Helvetica or Arial that is not embedded takes a system font instead.
- The ICC profile, iccs/ (CC0-1.0), read only by the WebAssembly colour
  management.
- Every WebAssembly binary: wasm/jbig2.wasm, wasm/openjpeg.wasm,
  wasm/qcms_bg.wasm and wasm/quickjs-eval.wasm, with QuickJS's
  wasm/quickjs-eval.js and the qcms and QuickJS licence files. The viewer
  runs pdf.js without WebAssembly (useWasm: false) and runs no PDF
  JavaScript.
- @napi-rs/canvas, pdfjs-dist's optional dependency: a canvas for pdf.js
  under Node, which the browser build never loads.
